<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Click the begin input of the first box and, without clicking anywhere else,
			type 2026/08/07.
		2. Reload, then Tab out of the textbox above into the box.

		- Expected: focusing an input focuses that input. The characters land in the input
			on the FIRST click, and tabbing in leaves the calendar closed.
		- Bug: the calendar opens the moment the input takes focus and moves focus into the
			role="dialog" popup, so the first click is lost and the keystrokes are eaten by
			the calendar's arrow-key handler.

		Opening the calendar is a separate, explicit gesture: the trigger button, or Alt+Up /
			Alt+Down on an input. Either arrow TOGGLES (same as datebox), so whichever one you
			press opens a closed calendar and closes an open one. The second box has no trigger
			button, so Alt+Up / Alt+Down is its only keyboard way in.

		Focusing an input rings the box; tabbing out again must remove the ring.
	</label>
	<textbox id="before" value="tab from here"/>
	<daterangebox id="drb" format="yyyy/MM/dd"/>
	<daterangebox id="drbNoButton" format="yyyy/MM/dd" buttonVisible="false"/>
</zk>
